[6] Theorem-facing readout
  New lemma target:
    Danger-count moment gate.  A strict LRC14 counterexample must have
    safe_mu=0, hence every feasible count-dual polynomial has nonpositive
    expectation.  Therefore any packet with a positive degree-R dual bound
    is discharged without locating the witness interval.
  What this pass found:
    The route is not a cheap pair/second-moment proof.  Named hard rows
    remain invisible through degree 6.  Degree 8/9 begins to separate
    positive rows from AP/GW; degree 13 recovers exact safe mass.
  How this differs from HYP-2968:
    HYP-2968 proves positivity by exact Q/R lift intervals.  This route
    forgets all lift geometry and asks whether the integer multiplicity
    distribution alone already forces a safe set.
  live next step: search for a universal degree <= 13 dual family
    on fixed-margin labelled packets, or prove why AP/GW are the only
    rows whose danger-count distribution defeats every low-degree dual.
